------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope of this NOTICE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains three original Solidity source files (clean
and planted twins) plus a differential Foundry harness. No upstream
Taiko source code, build configuration, prover artifacts, or contracts
are vendored or copied into this repository; the three files under
src/ are minimal demonstrations written from scratch against the
public specifications and documentation cited below. The contracts are
named "execution-layer mirrors" precisely to flag this: they mirror
behavior the public spec requires of a Type-1 execution layer; they
are not copies of any Taiko-Labs-authored source.

Forge-std is vendored as a pinned git submodule at lib/forge-std
(tag v1.9.4); no Foundry source is duplicated inside this repository.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream specifications and documentation referenced
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ethereum specification authors

  Ethereum Yellow Paper (Wood et al.). Appendix E ("Precompiled
  Contracts") is the canonical reference for the precompile-parity
  property exercised by src/PrecompileMirror.sol and the SHA-256
  branch of test/Equivalence.t.sol.
  https://ethereum.github.io/yellowpaper/paper.pdf

  EIP-2929 (Buterin, Swende), "Gas cost increases for state access
  opcodes." Source of the cold (2100) and warm (100) storage-access
  constants exercised by src/GasSchedule.sol and the gas-schedule
  branch of test/Equivalence.t.sol.
  https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-2929

  EIP-3529 and EIP-3651 are named in README.md's scope discussion as
  follow-on Type-1 surfaces; no source file in this repository
  depends on them yet.

NIST

  FIPS 180-4, "Secure Hash Standard," is the source of the canonical
  "abc" SHA-256 test vector used by test/Equivalence.t.sol.
  https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/fips/180/4/final

Taiko Labs

  Taiko documentation, "Multi-proofs" page (which carries the Type-1
  Ethereum-equivalence framing). Cited in README.md as the spec
  reference for the PrecompileParity case.
  https://docs.taiko.xyz/core-concepts/multi-proofs

  Taiko documentation, "Based contestable rollup" page. Cited in
  README.md as the spec reference for the BasedSequencingOrdering
  case (inclusion-list ordering rule).
  https://docs.taiko.xyz/core-concepts/based-contestable-rollup

  Taiko whitepaper. Sections "Why Type-1" and "Based Contestable
  Rollup" are cited in README.md to frame the Type-1 vs Type-2
  discriminator and the proposing / proving role decoupling.
  https://taiko.xyz/whitepaper.pdf

